{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_rails_monolith_decision", "label": "Decision \u2014 Build the POC as a Rails 8.x Monolith", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not because Ruby is fast, but because the epistemic domain model will change repeatedly as real evidence graphs expose weaknesses, and familiarity decides how quickly bad abstractions and subtle bugs get noticed. This file is the single home for stack rationale."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_topology", "label": "Topology \u2014 Two Containers, Postgres for Everything", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Solid Queue and Solid Cache live in PostgreSQL so development needs exactly two services and no Redis."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_distributed_research_centralized_coordination", "label": "Distributed Research, Centralized Coordination", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inference runs on contributors' hardware or accounts while the server does cheap deterministic work, so research throughput grows fast while central cost grows slowly."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_service_objects_not_callbacks", "label": "Service Objects, Not Callbacks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Epistemic logic in Active Record callbacks is not explicit, testable, replayable or extractable; an append plus an apply plus a recompute job is."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_projection_concern", "label": "Projection Concern \u2014 Validity Windows and active_at(seq)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rows carry created_seq and invalidated_seq and are readonly outside Ledger::Apply, which is what makes reproducing an earlier snapshot a query rather than a reconstruction."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_postgresql_no_graph_database", "label": "PostgreSQL, No Graph Database", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recursive CTEs, indexed edge tables, JSONB, full-text search and pg_trgm are enough for the POC and likely well beyond; pgvector only in P1 and only if trigram dedup proves inadequate."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_background_jobs_idempotent", "label": "Background Jobs \u2014 Idempotent and Keyed by (target, seq)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "So a retry or a replay never double-applies; recompute is incremental over only the claims whose counted links, evidence or groups changed at that seq."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_active_storage_content_hash_identity", "label": "Active Storage \u2014 Content Hash Is Identity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "sources.content_hash identifies the content and the blob key does not, so moving storage providers must not change any hash."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_caching_explicit_rows", "label": "Caching \u2014 Explicit Rows, Not Redis", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The real caches are claim_scores and summaries rows that can be deleted at any time and regenerated."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_extraction_contract_and_policy", "label": "Extraction Contract and Policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Do not extract because compiled languages feel serious or microservices are fashionable; consider it only when profiling shows sustained saturation and the savings exceed running another service. Any reimplementation must produce identical canonical traces on the golden fixtures."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_go_vs_rust", "label": "Go vs. Rust (if ever)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Go for service-shaped concurrent database-heavy work, Rust for CPU-bound or untrusted binary parsing. There is no requirement that either is ever introduced."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_performance_boundaries", "label": "Likely Future Hotspots", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scoring and recompute fan-out is the first candidate for extraction; task scheduling stays in Rails until measured otherwise."}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_operational_goal", "label": "Operational Goal \u2014 One Modest VM", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grow by pushing research compute outward before scaling anything central."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_rails_monolith_decision", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_topology", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/epistemic-ledger-poc-spec-v4/epistemic-ledger-poc/11-rails-architecture.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_11_rails_architecture_rails_monolith_decision", "target": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger